servation, day) are not enforced\", \"actual\": \"WELCOME10 ('10% off your first reservation') was accepted for a second reservation made in the same session after an earlier reservation already existed, violating the first-reservation rule. WEEKEND20 ('20% off weekend dining') was accepted for Aug 27, 2026, which is a Thursday (a weekday, not a weekend), violating the day-of-week eligibility rule. Only the GROUP15 party-size rule (6+ guests) was correctly enforced, rejecting it for a 2-guest reservation with the message 'This coupon requires a party of 6 or more.'\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Missing/invalid field information is not identified to the user\", \"actual\": \"Submitting the reservation form with all fields empty, or with an invalid email (e.g. 'bademail'), silently fails to create a reservation (confirmed no reservation appears in My Reservations) but shows no error text, toast, aria-invalid attribute, or visual indication of which field(s) are missing/invalid. Only focus moves to the Name field in the empty-form case.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Modify dialog opened, changes to time/party-size saved successfully via 'Save Changes'. Cancel button opened an alertdialog 'Cancel Reservation?' requiring explicit confirmation; clicking 'Keep Reservation' left both reservations unchanged, while clicking 'Cancel Reservation' actually cancelled it.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Creating a reservation showed an immediate toast ('Reservation Confirmed!') and confirmation panel, and it appeared instantly in Upcoming without reload. Modifying a reservation showed an immediate toast ('Reservation Updated') and the list reflected new time/party size instantly in the same session.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Upcoming tab and Past tab clearly separate reservations by status (Upcoming vs Cancelled). Each reservation card displays restaurant name, date, time, party size, status label, location (neighborhood, e.g. 'Little Italy'/'Warehouse District'), and applied coupon when present (e.g. 'Coupon applied: WEEKEND20'), both in Upcoming and Past/Cancelled views.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Restaurant list rating is inconsistent with detail page rating and does not update after new reviews\", \"actual\": \"Home page list shows a static seed rating per restaurant (e.g. The Golden Fork 4.8) which does not match the rating computed/shown on that restaurant's own detail page (4.5, derived from its 2 reviews) even before any new review was added. After submitting new reviews for Ember & Smoke (rating changed 5.0→4.5, count 1→2 on detail page) and Spice Route (rating became 3.0, count 1 on detail page), the home page restaurant list still displayed the original unchanged ratings (Ember & Smoke 4.7, Spice Route 4.4), showing the list summary is never refreshed from actual review data.\", \"evidence\": null}]}"
